 	Java 8 Features

1. Lambda Expressions
Allows writing anonymous functions with a shorter syntax.
It improves readability and supports functional programming in Java.


2. Functional Interface
An interface that contains only one abstract method.
It can be implemented using lambda expressions.


3. Stream API
Provides a way to process collections of data in a functional style.
It supports operations like filtering, mapping, and sorting.




4. Default Methods in Interfaces
Allows interfaces to have method implementations.
It helps add new methods without breaking existing implementations.


5. Static Methods in Interfaces
Allows static methods to be defined inside interfaces.
These methods are accessed using the interface name.

6. Method References
Provides a shorter way to call existing methods using :: operator.
It improves code readability when using lambda expressions.


7. Optional Class
A container object used to handle null values safely.
It helps avoid NullPointerException.


8. Date and Time API
Introduced new classes for handling date and time.
It provides better alternatives to the old Date and Calendar classes.


9. Nashorn JavaScript Engine
Allows Java applications to execute JavaScript code.
It provides better performance than the previous engine.

10. Collectors API
Provides methods to collect Stream results into collections.
It supports operations like grouping and joining data.


11. CompletableFuture
Supports asynchronous programming in Java.
It helps execute tasks in the background and handle results efficiently.


12. Base64 Encoding and Decoding
Provides built-in support for Base64 encoding and decoding.
It is available through the java.util.Base64 class.
  
  
  
  
  
  
  